WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:04.590
The search for the most immersive interactive
gameplay experience is over, but the fight

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.560
for survival has only just begun.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.660
In case you missed a few key details, here
are all the clues you need to puzzle out the

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.040
ending to Escape Room.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.840
The premise of Escape Room revolves around
a group of strangers who receive invites to

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.440
a competitive escape game, purportedly the
most immersive experience of its kind.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.090
The game is being put on by a company called
Minos Escape Rooms, a name that suggests this

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:27.580
company means business.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:32.520
The name "Minos" refers to the mythical first
King of Crete, who presided over a labyrinth

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.200
to which young people would be brought for
his entertainment.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.520
Maze-like and practically unescapable, the
participants would typically die inside the

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.980
labyrinth, killed by a monstrous Minotaur.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.760
While the movie's escape room isn't particularly
maze-like, the idea of people being lured

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.090
there to die for others' entertainment proves
especially relevant by the time the ending

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.420
rolls around, and the true nature of the company
is revealed.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.960
“Talk about immersive"
"what's wrong with you, that was real!"

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.000
After the escape game reveals its deadly nature,
the surviving players start to uncover what

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:05.310
its true purpose is.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:11.390
Mike, Ben, Zoey, and Jason enter a room that's
mocked up to resemble a hospital several hospitals,

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.200
actually, with each player finding something
familiar.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:18.780
They realize the setup is meant to remind
them of past traumatic experiences in which

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.620
they emerged as the lone survivors.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.640
Zoey survived a plane crash, Jason survived
a boating accident, Mike survived a mining

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.060
accident, and Ben survived a fatal drunk driving
collision.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.380
As Zoey describes it, they are all statistical
anomalies.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.260
This aspect of the game is more than just
psychological.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:40.160
As the game master reveals in the final chamber,
the contest was set up specifically to pit

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.690
lone survivors against each other, for the
sake of seeing what would happen when these

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.940
lucky few compete.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.040
Upon discovering the game's true nature, something

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.550
inside Zoey snaps.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.990
While all of the other players set about attempting
to solve a puzzle, Zoey goes berserk, and

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.180
starts smashing every camera in the room.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:00.060
She guesses that the people in charge of the
game aren't just observing their play, but

00:02:00.071 --> 00:02:04.170
actively involving themselves in it — something
that would be impossible if she takes away

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.160
their ability to watch.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.820
"They're watching us, they know every move
that we're making.”

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:13.160
As poisonous gas fills the room, the other
players flee, leaving Zoey behind as she insists

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.280
on finishing the job.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.670
She survives the gas by breathing through
an oxygen mask, knowing that no one can see

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:19.700
she's still alive.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:24.040
When the Minos staff comes to clear out the
chamber, they assume she's dead — until

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:24.740
she attacks.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.910
Danny, the avid gamer who met his end by drowning
in the cold room, previously insisted that

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:32.390
brute force shouldn't be necessary to win
the game.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.700
But in this instance, it might be the only
way.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.940
While Zoey practices her game-breaking gambit,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.440
Ben presses forward to the final room, where
he meets a man who describes himself as the

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.140
game master.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.000
Ben is declared the winner while the GM monologues
like a super villain, spilling all the details

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.590
of Minos' motivations.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:54.319
He reveals the games are entertainment for
wealthy audiences, like gladiator fights,

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.480
with Ben's group being the latest iteration
of a long line of twisted games.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.599
The contest, he reveals, is for the benefit
of no one but the viewers — the players

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:03.660
aren't allowed to win.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:08.920
The game master then attempts to strangle
Ben to death before Zoey reappears and intervenes.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.620
Together, they kill the game master, and finally
make their escape.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.360
After Ben and Zoey leave, 24 hours pass, with

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.880
Ben being checked into a hospital for his
injuries.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.700
When Zoey is informed that Ben is stable,
she's called away by police to assist in their

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.520
investigation.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.300
Their findings are not encouraging.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.800
Back at the Minos building, the company is
nowhere to be found.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.540
The facility has been cleared out.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.959
In a final insult, Zoey is taunted by a message
on the wall, familiar only to her, that reads

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.800
"Wootang Yu" — a mysterious name that previously
appeared in several rooms of the game.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.520
She realizes that the nonsense name is actually
an anagram that solves to "no way out.".

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.220
Six months later, Ben and Zoey catch up with

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.580
each other in Chicago.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:54.120
While life is going well for Ben, Zoey is
still seeking closure.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:58.290
The bodies of their fellow players, she discovers,
were scattered around the world, with their

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.250
deaths made to look like accidents.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:04.610
The scheme sits poorly with Zoey's sense of
justice — the world deserves to know what

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.480
really happened.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:10.460
Zoey manages to convince Ben to fly to Minos'
Manhattan headquarters, the coordinates of

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.780
which she discovered hidden in the company's
logo.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.700
They book a flight to the city — but it
turns out Minos has been watching, and is

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.010
already one step ahead.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:22.600
In an epilogue, it's revealed that the people
behind Minos have designed a custom-made escape

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.420
game just for the two of them, which they
plan to install on their flight.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:30.840
They will apparently have only a 4% chance
of surviving this game, which seems to be

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.830
targeting them out of pure spite.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:37.400
On a monitor, a shadowy silhouette figure
overseeing the operation says it's time to

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.000
play again.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.380
Jigsaw would be proud.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.120
Escape Room ends with a clear tease for a

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.949
sequel — one that could demonstrate the
truly awesome reach of Minos.

00:04:45.949 --> 00:04:50.060
It's the only time that viewers get a real
glimpse behind the curtain, and the operation

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.080
looks massive.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:55.419
Dozens of people are involved with the design
of the plane escape game alone, which makes

00:04:55.419 --> 00:04:57.670
you wonder just how deep the rabbit hole goes.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:02.910
Who is the shadowy figure overseeing the game,
and what is the motivation behind the conspiracy?

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.920
Is really just for entertainment, or could
it be something more?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.200
Whatever may come next, the track has been
laid for some truly off-the-rails insanity.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:13.920
If a sequel gets the greenlight, you can count
us in the game.

